From 502d19c8a1ed5905c09e2a66c8ea796ac54975e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 07:21:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firstboot: kill dual credential-surface dead-end on factory
 reset

Field report (GT-BE98 v2.1.2, reproduces on all models): after a factory
reset the login lands on the stock Main_Password.asp, that page changes the
admin password, then the Reaper first-run gate forces Reaper_FirstBoot.asp
whose second chpass fails ("Could not apply credentials") because the
password is no longer default and no current credential is supplied. User is
stranded and must restore stock firmware to recover.

Root cause: two credential-change surfaces were both live on first boot. The
stock login-CGI meta-refresh (web.c) sent a default-password box to
Main_Password.asp, which does NOT load state.js, so the Reaper first-run gate
could never reclaim it; meanwhile get_index_page() + state.js independently
force Reaper_FirstBoot.asp. The two race and the second chpass dead-ends.

Fix: unify on the single themed Reaper surface.
- web.c login-CGI: on default-pw / force_chgpass, redirect to
  Reaper_FirstBoot.asp when the theme is on and the file exists (stock
  Main_Password.asp kept as fallback for theme-off / missing-file).
- Main_Password.asp: early <head> guard hands off to Reaper_FirstBoot.asp on
  a default-pw / force_chgpass box (defense-in-depth, since this page omits
  state.js). Later password changes (pw already set) fall through untouched,
  so Administration / AiMesh re-use is unaffected.

Reaper_FirstBoot now runs first while creds are still default, so its chpass
succeeds. No version bump (rides the v2.1.3 rung). Metal owed: GT-BE98 +
RT-BE96U factory-reset first boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/httpd/web.c           | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 release/src/router/www/Main_Password.asp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
index b4d84e4f9b..de94362c65 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
@@ -25304,8 +25304,26 @@ login_cgi(webs_t wp, char_t *url, int auth_version)
 
 			websWrite(wp,"<HTML><HEAD>\n" );
 #ifndef RTCONFIG_BCM_MFG
-			if((is_passwd_default() && !nvram_match(ATE_FACTORY_MODE_STR(), "1")) || nvram_get_int("force_chgpass"))
-				websWrite(wp, T("<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0; url=Main_Password.asp\">\r\n"));
+			if((is_passwd_default() && !nvram_match(ATE_FACTORY_MODE_STR(), "1")) || nvram_get_int("force_chgpass")) {
+				/* reaper: the first-boot credential change is owned by the themed
+				 * Reaper_FirstBoot.asp, NOT the stock Main_Password.asp. Shipping both
+				 * left two credential surfaces racing on a factory box: this stock
+				 * login redirect landed on Main_Password.asp (which does NOT load
+				 * state.js, so the Reaper first-run gate could never reclaim it), that
+				 * page changed the admin password, and the Reaper gate (get_index_page
+				 * / state.js) THEN forced Reaper_FirstBoot.asp whose second chpass
+				 * failed auth - the password was no longer default and no current
+				 * credential was supplied -> "Could not apply credentials" dead-end
+				 * (field report GT-BE98 v2.1.2, all models). Route straight to the
+				 * single Reaper surface while creds are still default; fall back to the
+				 * stock page only when the theme is off or the file is absent. */
+				const char *ri_fb = nvram_get("reaper_inject");
+				int reaper_on_fb = !(ri_fb && *ri_fb && atoi(ri_fb) == 0);
+				if(reaper_on_fb && check_if_file_exist("/www/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp"))
+					websWrite(wp, T("<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0; url=Reaper_FirstBoot.asp\">\r\n"));
+				else
+					websWrite(wp, T("<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0; url=Main_Password.asp\">\r\n"));
+			}
 			else
 #endif
 			{
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Main_Password.asp b/release/src/router/www/Main_Password.asp
index 71207724b2..17eba9a371 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Main_Password.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Main_Password.asp
@@ -7,6 +7,22 @@
 <meta HTTP-EQUIV="Pragma" CONTENT="no-cache">
 <meta HTTP-EQUIV="Expires" CONTENT="-1">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, user-scalable=no">
+<script>
+/* reaper: first-boot credential change belongs to Reaper_FirstBoot.asp. This stock page
+   does NOT load state.js, so the Reaper first-run gate can never bounce it - a factory box
+   redirected here would run the stock dual-submit (chpass + saveNvram + QIS_wizard hop) and
+   collide with the Reaper credential surface, dead-ending on "Could not apply credentials".
+   Guard here as early as possible: on a default-password / force_chgpass box hand straight
+   off to the single Reaper surface. Later password changes (pw already set) fall through to
+   the normal stock page, so AiMesh / Administration re-use is unaffected. */
+(function(){
+	try{
+		var pwDef = ('<% check_pw(); %>' == '1');
+		var fchg  = ('<% nvram_get("force_chgpass"); %>' == '1');
+		if(pwDef || fchg){ location.replace('/Reaper_FirstBoot.asp'); }
+	}catch(e){}
+})();
+</script>
 <link rel="shortcut icon" href="images/favicon.png">
 <link rel="icon" href="images/favicon.png">
 <title>ASUS Login</title>
-- 
2.25.1

